    "labelChirho": "Shebna (proper name)",
    "descriptionChirho": "A Hebrew proper name (שֶׁבְנָא) referring to a royal official during King Hezekiah's reign, variously identified as 'over the house' (palace steward) and later as secretary/scribe. All 9 occurrences (Isaiah 22:15; 36:3,11,22; 37:2; 2 Kings 18:18,26,37; 19:2) refer to the same individual. The two clusters differ only in the presence/absence of the conjunction waw ('and Shebna' vs. 'Shebna'), a surface grammatical feature, not a semantic distinction. Evidence: eng 'Shebna / and Shevnah,' spa 'Sebna / y Sebna,' arb 'شِبْنَا / وَشَبْنَا,' kor '셸브나 / 솁나,' swa 'Shebna / na Shebna,' hin 'शेबना / और शेब्नाह.'",
